Preflight: impact run 2026-10-01 on 9860e3e (scratch worktree, rough stand-ins for all seven BPM stories applied together) - 14076 passed / 21 skipped / 1 failed with AGENTS_DIR=agents/ as CI sets it. The one failure (tests/unit/test_remote_sync.py::test_ssh_run_raises_called_process_error_for_unreachable_host) is host-only: the preflight container has no ssh binary, and it fails identically on untouched master there. 0 conflicts with pre-existing tests. `ruff check .` clean (0.16.8); scripts/check_line_limit.py OK (tests/benchmark/harness.py 876 -> 886 lines). The tests/benchmark self-suite (NOT run by CI; pyproject addopts ignores tests/benchmark) has 18 pre-existing failures on master and none new.

TARGET IMPLEMENTER: on-device (~20B class). Pin: backend "ollama", model "gpt-oss-20b-high:latest". Two production files (tests/benchmark/models.py, tests/benchmark/README.md), zero new functions: three new dict entries and three README table rows.

WHY
The published benchmark compares three routing arms. Arm A is the existing "sonnet" entry and needs no change. This story adds Arm B and the on-device Arm C at two step budgets. The existing "gptoss_claude_review" entry inherits PIPELINE_LOCAL_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=900 from _LOCAL_AGENT_ENV, which a 120-step run would hit before its step cap, so both new on-device entries use 1800 and differ ONLY in PIPELINE_LOCAL_MAX_STEPS.

EDIT 1 - tests/benchmark/models.py. Use str_replace. OLD (matches exactly once):
    # --- cloud (claude CLI) ---
NEW (the three entries, then the original line unchanged):
    # --- published matrix arms (tests/benchmark/run_published_matrix.sh) ---
    # Arm B: a cloud open-weight model implements, Claude reviews.
    "glm_claude_review": {
        "mock": False,
        "env": {
            **_local(os.environ.get("BENCH_GLM_DISPATCH_TAG", "glm-5.3-flash:cloud"),
                     temperature="0.3", num_ctx="32768")["env"],
            "PIPELINE_LOCAL_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS": "1800",
            "PIPELINE_BACKEND_REVIEW": "claude",
        },
    },
    # Arm C at the shipped step budget (60) and at double it (120). Same
