    },
    # --- cloud (claude CLI) ---

EDIT 2 - tests/benchmark/README.md, "## Models" table: add one row per new entry (glm_claude_review, gptoss_claude_review_s60, gptoss_claude_review_s120), each with 3 cells matching the table's existing 3 columns (Name | Backend | Notes). Keep every existing row unchanged.

DO NOT CHANGE (survivor list): every existing MODELS entry, especially "sonnet", "gptoss_claude_review" and "gptoss_temp03"; _LOCAL_AGENT_ENV; _local(); _local_arm(); _local_provider(). Do not touch any other file.

WHERE TESTS GO: pyproject.toml's addopts has --ignore=tests/benchmark, so tests under tests/benchmark/ are NOT collected by the suite or CI and cannot grade this story. Put every new test in tests/unit/ (file named below) and import the bench module the way tests/unit/test_bench_pytest_gitignore_covers_venv_symlink.py does (`from tests.benchmark import <module>`). Do not edit or add files under tests/benchmark/test_*.py. SCOPE NOTE: the pipeline classifies every path under tests/ as a test file, so this story's `files` is [] (no production file may change) and the tests/benchmark/ tooling files named below are AUTHORIZED edits even though the classifier calls them tests. They are benchmark tooling, not test assertions; say "benchmark tooling edit authorized by the plan" in the commit message.

TESTS TO WRITE FIRST: tests/unit/test_bench_published_arms.py (`from tests.benchmark import models`). Assert only what this story adds (MODELS is cumulative; never assert its total size or full key list):
- each of the three names is in models.MODELS and has "mock" False;
- all three set PIPELINE_BACKEND_REVIEW == "claude" and PIPELINE_LOCAL_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_SECONDS == "1800";
- glm_claude_review's PIPELINE_LOCAL_MODEL_DEFAULT == "glm-5.3-flash:cloud" when BENCH_GLM_DISPATCH_TAG is unset (reload the module under monkeypatch.delenv) and equals the override when it is set;
- the s60 and s120 env dicts are identical except PIPELINE_LOCAL_MAX_STEPS ("60" vs "120") - compute the differing keys and assert the set is exactly {"PIPELINE_LOCAL_MAX_STEPS"};
- negative: the pre-existing "gptoss_claude_review" entry still has PIPELINE_LOCAL_MAX_STEPS "60" and timeout "900" (this story must not change it); "sonnet" still has PIPELINE_BACKEND_DISPATCH "claude".

DONE WHEN: the new test file passes, `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` passes, `.venv/bin/python -m ruff check .` is clean.
